{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00063",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.52,
      "end_seconds": 5.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Hi there, is it alright if I come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.38,
      "end_seconds": 10.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "That's alright, take a seat. Tell me why you've come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.49,
      "end_seconds": 20.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.58,
      "text": "Um, so... a dry cough that won't go away. That's why I came. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.48,
      "end_seconds": 22.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.85,
      "end_seconds": 30.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "About... well, about a month. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.94,
      "end_seconds": 33.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Is there anything that triggers it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.36,
      "end_seconds": 38.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "I notice it more with after meals and lying down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.58,
      "end_seconds": 46.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Does it happen all the time or in spells?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.1,
      "end_seconds": 50.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "I'd say a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.5,
      "end_seconds": 54.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.58,
      "end_seconds": 62.37,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly. I've had a hoarse voice in the mornings too, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.99,
      "end_seconds": 64.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "What about wheezing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.51,
      "end_seconds": 66.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "No wheezing, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.26,
      "end_seconds": 71.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Have you had any coughing up blood, weight loss or night sweats?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.76,
      "end_seconds": 77.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "No coughing up blood, weight loss or night sweats, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.34,
      "end_seconds": 82.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.09,
      "end_seconds": 83.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.72,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.3,
      "end_seconds": 97.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.97,
      "end_seconds": 101.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Just my tonsils out, when I was a child."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.96,
      "end_seconds": 105.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.5,
      "end_seconds": 108.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.67,
      "end_seconds": 114.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.98,
      "end_seconds": 122.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "I'm, I'm on losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day. Digene. I take it after meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.27,
      "end_seconds": 128.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Just to be sure I've got this right, the losartan, what dose was that again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.56,
      "end_seconds": 130.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "50 milligrams. Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.19,
      "end_seconds": 136.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "So, what about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.56,
      "end_seconds": 139.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "My father had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.36,
      "end_seconds": 143.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.64,
      "end_seconds": 144.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.92,
      "end_seconds": 150.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.82,
      "end_seconds": 151.56,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.42,
      "end_seconds": 157.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.43,
      "end_seconds": 160.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.49,
      "end_seconds": 163.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.73,
      "end_seconds": 169.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.91,
      "end_seconds": 175.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.66,
      "end_seconds": 179.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.84,
      "end_seconds": 180.58,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.07,
      "end_seconds": 199.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.83,
      "end_seconds": 211.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.14,
      "end_seconds": 236.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.09,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 77, SpO2 99 percent on room air. And respiratory rate 16, temp 36.9 degrees, blood pressure 124 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.63,
      "end_seconds": 239.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.29,
      "end_seconds": 246.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment. Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.66,
      "end_seconds": 249.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "No problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.76,
      "end_seconds": 255.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.55,
      "end_seconds": 258.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.64,
      "end_seconds": 278.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Chest is clear and the throat looks a little red at the back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.68,
      "end_seconds": 294.72,
      "duration_seconds": 14.04,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.99,
      "end_seconds": 298.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.7,
      "end_seconds": 313.6,
      "duration_seconds": 11.9,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with a cough driven by acid reflux. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.2,
      "end_seconds": 316.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.64,
      "end_seconds": 337.34,
      "duration_seconds": 19.7,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a cough driven by acid reflux is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a dry cough that won't go away for about a month, mild, and no wheezing or weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.9,
      "end_seconds": 340.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.24,
      "end_seconds": 346.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.38,
      "end_seconds": 358.64,
      "duration_seconds": 11.26,
      "text": "Yeah, yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.21,
      "end_seconds": 362.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange breathing tests for chronic cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.43,
      "end_seconds": 366.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.12,
      "end_seconds": 392.41,
      "duration_seconds": 24.29,
      "text": "Let's use pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, for four weeks. That should help with reflux. Don't eat for two or three hours before lying down, and raise the head of the bed a little. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.93,
      "end_seconds": 402.57,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Let's review you in a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.88,
      "end_seconds": 404.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.24,
      "end_seconds": 410.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Let me check that I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.69,
      "end_seconds": 418.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "So, I take the pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast and come back in a month. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 420.02,
      "end_seconds": 425.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's all I have. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.81,
      "end_seconds": 428.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    }
  ]
}